e-restart protocol is strong: it captures a healthy pre-restart service and boot identity, restart scheduling and temporary SSH unavailability, a changed post-restart boot identity corroborated by lifecycle observations, and recovered service, content, account/session, and namespace state.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor listening-sockets observation is empty despite the immediately preceding direct command showing an active :::8080 listener and successful HTTP response. Because the lifecycle socket observation was also empty at baseline despite active SSH access, its socket coverage appears limited, but the discrepancy prevents maximum confidence.","There is no cluster state to assess because the managed topology contains only one standalone node."]}
